{"content_type": "text/xml", "decision_time": "2026-04-22", "fetch_kind": "actual_http_get", "fetched_at": "2026-07-29T19:13:06+00:00", "final_url": "https://www.ecfr.gov/api/versioner/v1/full/2026-04-22/title-21.xml?part=101&section=101.91", "metadata_sha256": "3c518412f131056f16034b4bd03756277c76b16e72af660e2f54ea1caf28ca66", "raw_content_sha256": "886de24e958286e29b90a2f1fc68357b73618e76849b2895de2b965636cb086f", "raw_path": "private/web_snapshots/raw/d943047e65b3f0ca8cb92a0a62a3ac79311ac7bcd3c61e97b96020d004826d21.response", "raw_size_bytes": 5913, "requested_url": "https://www.ecfr.gov/api/versioner/v1/full/2026-04-22/title-21.xml?part=101&section=101.91", "response_headers": {"content-type": "text/xml", "date": "Wed, 29 Jul 2026 19:13:06 GMT"}, "source_topic": "food_nutrition", "status_code": 200, "support_excerpt": "The labeling claim \"gluten-free\" means: (i) That the food bearing the claim in its labeling: (A) Does not contain any one of the following: ( 1 ) An ingredient that is a gluten-containing grain (e.g., spelt wheat); ( 2 ) An ingredient that is derived from a gluten-containing grain and that has not been processed to remove gluten (e.g., wheat flour); or ( 3 ) An ingredient that is derived from a gluten-containing grain and that has been processed to remove gluten (e.g., wheat starch), if the use of that ingredient results in the presence of 20 parts per million (ppm) or more gluten in the food", "support_excerpt_verified_in_normalized_dom_text": true, "support_excerpts": ["The labeling claim \"gluten-free\" means: (i) That the food bearing the claim in its labeling: (A) Does not contain any one of the following: ( 1 ) An ingredient that is a gluten-containing grain (e.g., spelt wheat); ( 2 ) An ingredient that is derived from a gluten-containing grain and that has not been processed to remove gluten (e.g., wheat flour); or ( 3 ) An ingredient that is derived from a gluten-containing grain and that has been processed to remove gluten (e.g., wheat starch), if the use of that ingredient results in the presence of 20 parts per million (ppm) or more gluten in the food", "A food that bears the claim \"gluten-free\" in its labeling and fails to meet the requirements of paragraph (a)(3) of this section and, if applicable, paragraphs (c)(2) through (4) of this section will be deemed misbranded"], "support_text_normalization": "html_entity_unescape+unicode_quote_dash_fold+whitespace_collapse+casefold", "task_id": "SWOR085", "text_encoding": "UTF-8", "verified_as_of": "2026-07-29"}
